            "new_string": "### 51.2 Three-tier scan pipeline: rules → local disambig → minimal LLM\n- [ ] Restructure the scan-to-fix pipeline into three explicit tiers\n      to push resolution as far left as possible.\n  - Tier 1 (deterministic): all rule-based checks run without LLM.\n    Punctuation, fullwidth/halfwidth, case, known vocabulary, MoE\n    orthography, CJK-Latin spacing, exclusion zones.  Already the\n    default path; goal is to ensure NO ambiguous-but-resolvable cases\n    leak to Tier 3.\n  - Tier 2 (local disambiguation): before invoking LLM, run a local\n    ambiguity scorer on each unresolved term:\n    1. Neighbor-word heuristic: if surrounding ±40 chars contain\n       domain keywords (scheduler, PID, thread → \"行程\"), resolve\n       locally.  Reuse existing `context_clues` infrastructure.\n    2. Profile-based preference: `ui_strings` and `strict_moe` have\n       strong priors; use profile-specific preferred-term tables.\n    3. Fixed collocation: compound terms like \"render pipeline\",\n       \"process table\" resolve deterministically.\n    Build an `AmbiguityScore { score: f32, resolved: Option<String> }`.\n    Only terms with score in the gray zone (configurable threshold,\n    default 0.3-0.7) proceed to Tier 3.\n  - Tier 3 (minimal-context LLM): send only span-level classification\n    requests, NOT full text.  Prompt schema:\n    ```json\n    { \"term\": \"process\", \"profile\": \"default\",\n      \"domain_hint\": \"os_kernel\",\n      \"left_context\": \"...\", \"right_context\": \"...\",\n      \"candidates\": [\"行程\",\"流程\",\"處理程序\"],\n      \"output\": {\"choice\":\"\",\"confidence\":0.0,\"reason\":\"\"} }\n    ```\n    Forbid full-text rewrite.  Model answers a classification question.\n  - Scope: new `src/engine/disambig.rs` (Tier 2 scorer),\n    `src/mcp/sampling.rs` (Tier 3 prompt restructure),\n    `src/mcp/tools.rs` (pipeline orchestration).\n  - Gate: on a corpus with 20 ambiguous terms, ≥60% resolved at\n    Tier 2