們有理由相信`, `拭目以待`,\n      `值得期待`.  Without 35.7 the \"section-terminal\" gate cannot\n      be enforced reliably.\n    - S4 mechanical bullet lists: flag a Markdown list (35.7)\n      where every item starts with `**` + keyword + `**`/`：`/`—`.\n    - S5 excessive bold: count `**...**` runs per Markdown\n      paragraph; flag when ≥3 per 200 chars.\n    - S6 em-dash overuse: count `——` per paragraph; flag at ≥1\n      per paragraph (the source explicitly says one per paragraph\n      is already a pattern, not >1).\n    - S7 formulaic \"despite\": `儘管.*挑戰` (≤40 chars) +\n      forward-looking verb (`仍然.*發展`, `持續.*繁榮`,\n      `蓬勃發展`) within one sentence (37.1).\n    - S8 false ranges: `從.*到.*再到` chains where the spans are\n      not on a meaningful scale.  Hard to detect automatically;\n      start with a finite list of known false-range openers and\n      require the chain to span ≥30 chars.\n  - Phase 3 — V3 copula avoidance (`作為`, `扮演`, `代表`, `象徵`,\n    `標誌著`) as context-gated `ai_filler` entries.  Needs\n    `negative_context_clues` for legitimate uses (`作為` meaning\n    \"in the capacity of\", `代表` as a noun for a delegate).\n    Cross-check with any existing `作為` vocabulary rule.\n    Coordinate with 53.2.Phase1 V2 to avoid double-flagging the\n    same span — pick one owner per pattern.\n  - Phase 4 — Meta/formatting (M1–M4) under context-string\n    discrimination \"AI meta:\":\n    - M1 chatbot artifacts: `希望這對你有幫助`, `讓我來為你`,\n      standalone `以下是` intro lines.\n    - M2 emoji as bullet markers: detect `^[\\p{Emoji}]\\s+\\*\\*` in\n      Markdown list items.\n    - M3 numbered paragraphs that should be prose: flag a numbered\n      list where every item is one sentence and the sentences read\n      as continuous prose (≥3 items, no nested bullets).  Best\n      effort heuristic.\n    - M4 markup artifacts: `oaicite`, `contentReference`,\n      `turn0search0`, `utm_source=chatgpt.com`, `utm_source=copilot.com`,\n      stray `**text**` in plaintext outputs.  These are highest\n      precision and lowest cost — implement first.\n  - Coverage gate (relaxed): of the 25 humanize checklist items,\n    Phases 1+3 cover C1–C5, C7, V1–V3, V6 (10 items, ~40%);\n    Phase 2 covers S1–S8 (8 items, ~32%) once 53.0 lands;\n    Phase 4 covers M1–M4 (4 items, ~16%).  Acknowledged gaps:\n    C6 (detail regression — requires comparing rewrite against\n    source, not in scope for a single-document linter), V4 (elegant\n    variation — requires semantic similarity over the whole document),\n    V5 (present participle chains — Chinese lacks participles, the\n    `了`-chain heuristic is too noisy to implement first cut).\n    Document these in a per-item mapping table inside the ruleset.\n  - Composite score interaction (40.11): structural and meta hits\n    feed the existing composite in `src/engine/ai_score.rs` via the\n    context-string discrimination above.  No `IssueType` schema\n    change required.  Re-evaluate if a future consumer needs\n    machine-readable subcategorization.\n  - Reference corpus: humanize SKILL.md Before/After pairs (MIT,\n    tzengyuxio/skills) into `tests/fixtures/humanize/` with a\n    `README.md` recording provenance, upstream commit, and\n    license.  Both projects are MIT — compatible.\n  - Scope: `assets/ruleset.json` (Phase 1+3+4 entries),\n    `src/engine/scan/grammar.rs` (Phase 2 detectors, gated on 53.0),\n    `src/engine/ai_score.rs` (no schema change, optional weighting\n    bump for `\"AI structural:\"` context-prefix hits),\n    `tests/fixtures/humanize/`.\n  - Per-item mapping table: maintained in `assets/ruleset.json`\n    metadata (`source: \"humanize.C1\"` etc.) so coverage can be\n    audited mechanically.\n\n### 53.2 Translationese (`翻譯腔` / 歐化) detection dimension\n- [ ] Currently the scanner has no dedicated detector for Europeanized\n      Chinese syntax.  The dewesternise checklist (25 items: G1–G8,\n      V1–V14, S1–S3) is distilled from 余光中's《論中文之西化》,\n      《從西而不化到西而化之》, and standard 歐化中文 literature.\n      Unlike AI filler detection (which is lexical), 翻譯腔 is\n      primarily a syntactic phenomenon: passive voice overuse,\n      abstract subjects, weak-verb decomposition, long pre-modifiers,\n      copula calques.  This warrants a new linting dimension parallel\n      to AI detection.\n  - Naming: `RuleType::Translationese` (matches existing\n    category-noun pattern: `Variant`, `Confusable`, `AiFiller`).\n    Not `Westernised` (British spelling) or `Westernized`.  Module\n    name follows: `src/engine/translationese_score.rs`.\n  - Orthogonality: the translationese score must NOT collapse into\n    the AI score.  A translated technical manual is 歐化 but not\n    AI-generated.  Report on a separate output channel; expose as a\n    distinct CLI/MCP field.\n  - Enum strategy: `RuleType::Translationese` is additive on the\n    serde side but breaks every exhaustive `RuleType` match site\n    (`src/engine/scan/rule_ir.rs:310`, `src/engine/scan/spelling.rs:72`,\n    `src/rules/ruleset.rs:353,698`).  Plan to update all of them in\n    the same commit that adds the variant; do not split across PRs.\n  - Phase 1 — Lexical subset (fits existing rule engine, no prereqs):\n    - G5 `們` plural overuse on non-human nouns (`政府們`, `書們`,\n      `國家們`).  Negative clues for vocatives (`老師們`,\n      `同學們`, `女士們`, `先生們`).  REPORT-ONLY by default;\n      see Phase 4.\n    - G6 `和` overuse: `(動詞|形容詞)和(動詞|形容詞)` in\n      contexts where 頓號 or asyndeton is preferred.  Hard to\n      detect without POS — start with a finite list of common\n      verb pairs (`唱歌和跳舞`, `學習和工作`).\n    - G7 `當.*的時候` calque — flag `當` followed within ≤15\n      chars by `的時候`/`時`.\n    - G8 pronoun overuse: ≥3 consecutive sentences in one\n      paragraph beginning with `他`/`她`/`它`/`他們`.  Density\n      check, not per-occurrence.\n    - V1 calque prepositions: `關於` at sentence head followed\n      by `,`/`，` within 20 chars; `由於.*的原因` (≤15 chars\n      between); `在.*方面`; `就.*而言`.  Gated by sentence-initial\n      position to reduce noise.\n    - V2 `作為一(個|名|位)` at sentence head — \"as a X\".\n      Coordinate ownership with 53.1.Phase3.\n    - V3 `透過` used with abstract means.  `negative_context_clues`:\n      `玻璃`, `縫隙`, `窗戶`, `屏幕`, `布料` (literal \"through\").\n    - V4 `的`-string redundancy (lexical layer only): runs of\n      `X的Y的Z的` ≥3 `的` in one NP-like span without internal\n      punctuation.  Distinct from S3 long pre-modifier (which\n      requires sentence index).\n    - V5 `一個` redundancy: `是一個` + adjective.  REPORT-ONLY by\n      default; see Phase 4.\n    - V6 `性` suffix overuse: `(危險|可行|合理|藝術|可能|必要)性`\n      in non-academic contexts.  Negative clues: `論文`, `研究`,\n      `分析` nearby (academic register).\n    - V8 literal adverb: `更好地`, `有效地`, `主要地`, `成功地`,\n      `深入地`.  Gated by following verb.\n    - V9 `這樣一個` outright.\n    - V10 weak verb + nominalization: explicit pair list rather\n      than regex — `(進行|展開|作出|給予|加以|予以|提供)` followed\n      within ≤4 chars by one of `(討論|調查|反應|決定|貢獻|檢討|\n      投票|分析|研究|改革|處理|支援|協助)`.  ~40 hand-curated\n      pairs from 余光中's list.  REPORT-ONLY by default.\n    - V11 vocabulary blunting: hard to detect mechanically (the\n      problem is that `選擇` is wrong because `不得不` is right);\n      defer to Phase 5 with a synonym thesaurus.  Document as\n      explicitly out of Phase 1 scope.\n    - V12 `最.*之一`: flag and suggest removal of `之一` when no\n      enumeration follows within ≤40 chars.  False-positive guard\n      for academic citations: negative clue `等` after `之一`.\n    - V14 `有著`, `存在著`, `有.{0,6}的發生` existential calques.\n    - S1 semantic overlap: finite list — `提前預告`, `互相合作`,\n      `繼續延續`, `共同協作`, `正在進行中`, `相互交流`, `預先準備`,\n      `事先預告`, `公開公告`.  Direct spelling rules.\n    - S2 scientific term overuse: `關注程度`, `重視度`, `強度高`\n      in non-academic prose.  Same academic-register negative\n      clues as V6.\n  - Phase 2 — Syntactic detectors (BLOCKED on 53.0):\n    - G1 passive voice density: count `被` per paragraph; flag\n      when density >2/100 chars.  Per-occurrence flagging only\n      when the surrounding verb has a natural active rewrite\n      (`被廣泛認為`, `被視為`, `被稱為`).\n      WHITELIST (technical zh-TW): `被定義為`, `被廣泛採用`,\n      `被置於`, `被稱作`, `被觀察到`, `被記錄為` (scientific/math\n      register).  Configurable per-domain in Phase 3.\n    - G2 abstract subject: noun phrase ending in\n      `的(減少|增加|提高|下降|通過|實施)` at sentence head\n      followed by `導致|標誌著|意味著`.  Requires sentence\n      boundary (37.1).\n    - G3/G4 displaced conditionals: `如果.*的話` or\n      `(如果|假如|若)` appearing after the main clause within\n      one sentence (37.1).  Suggest fronting.\n    - G8 (canonical 余光中 marker) copula + classifier inflation:\n      `他是一(個|名|位).*?的.*人` within one sentence — flag and\n      suggest deletion of copula/classifier.\n    - G9 (canonical 余光中 marker) `的`/`地` confusion:\n      Adjective + `的` + Verb where `地` is correct.  Hard\n      without POS; start with a finite list of common\n      adjective-adverb confusions (`仔細的看`, `認真的聽`,\n      `慢慢的走`).\n    - S3 long pre-modifier `的`-chain: recursive `的` counter\n      within one sentence (37.1) with no comma between — flag\n      when ≥4 `的` occur in one continuous span.  This is\n      余光中's `的的不休` phenomenon.\n    - V7 `.地` overuse on disyllabic adverbs (`慢慢地`, `靜靜地`,\n      `認真地`).  Finite whitelist.  AUTO-FIX SAFE on the\n      whitelist only.\n    - V13 tense marker overuse: multiple `(曾|已|過|了)` in one\n      sentence when explicit date already present.  Density\n      check, not per-occurrence.\n  - Phase 3a — Scoring module (BLOCKED on 53.0 + Phase 2):\n    - New `src/engine/translationese_score.rs`: composite score\n      from passive density, `的`-chain depth, weak-verb count,\n      pronoun density per 1000 chars.\n    - Orthogonal to `ai_score.rs` — separate output struct,\n      separate weight tuning, separate threshold.\n    - Per-domain calibration: `technical`, `literary`, `news`\n      profiles with different thresholds (technical zh-TW\n      tolerates more passive and `之一`).\n  - Phase 3b — CLI surface:\n    - `lint --detect-translationese` (parallel to `--detect-ai`).\n    - Combined flag `--detect-style` runs both, but reports two\n      separate score blocks.\n    - Per-domain flag: `--profile=technical|literary|news`.\n  - Phase 3c — MCP + ruleset config:\n    - MCP `zhtw` tool option `detect_translationese: bool`,\n      separate from `detect_ai`.\n    - `translationese_detection: bool` in\n      `src/rules/ruleset.rs` config struct, default off.\n    - Schema impact: `RuleType::Translationese` variant addition\n      lands here, with all match-arm updates in the same commit.\n  - Phase 4 — Fixer integration (narrow auto-fix surface):\n    - AUTO-FIX SAFE (whitelist-only): `V7 地` drop on the\n      disyllabic-adverb whitelist; `V9 這樣一個` → `這麼`;\n      `S1` semantic overlap pairs (exact match only).\n    - REPORT-ONLY (context-dependent, both reviewers agreed):\n      - `G5 們` — non-human noun detection requires POS tagging\n        the project does not have.\n      - `V5 一個` — mandatory in counting contexts (`只有一個`,\n        `第一個`).  Cannot drop safely without parse context.\n      - `V10` weak-verb collapses — collocational, not universal;\n        rhythm and emphasis change matters in formal prose.\n      - All Phase 2 syntactic detectors (passive, abstract subject,\n        displaced conditional, `的`-chain).\n    - Ship `auto_fix_safe: false` for the report-only set, with\n      a `suggested_rewrite` field that the user applies manually.\n  - Phase 5 (deferred) — V11 vocabulary blunting via a synonym\n    thesaurus.  Out of scope for the initial cut.\n  - Coverage gate (relaxed, with explicit gaps):\n    - Phase 1 covers G5, G6, G7, G8, V1–V10 (excluding V11), V12,\n      V14, S1, S2 (~16 items / 64%).\n    - Phase 2 covers G1, G2, G3/G4, G8 (余光中), G9 (余光中), S3,\n      V7, V13 (~7 additional items / 28%) once 53.0 lands.\n    - Acknowledged gaps: V11 deferred to Phase 5.\n    - Per-item mapping table maintained in `assets/ruleset.json`\n      metadata (`source: \"dewesternise.G1\"` etc.) so coverage\n      can be audited mechanically.\n    - Final gate: `--detect-translationese` on a clean zh-TW\n      technical document (project README, technical spec) produces\n      ≤1 false positive per 1000 characters under the `technical`\n      profile.\n  - Reference corpus: dewesternise SKILL.md Before/After pairs\n    (MIT, tzengyuxio/skills) into `tests/fixtures/translationese/`\n    with a `README.md` recording provenance, upstream commit, and\n    license.  Both projects are MIT — compatible.  Do NOT ship\n    余光中's copyrighted text; paraphrase canonical examples only\n    and cite the essays as theoretical grounding in comments.\n  - Interaction with existing P2 vocabulary rules: passive `被`,\n    `作為`, `透過` already have rule-level entries in P2.  Strategy\n    to avoid double-flagging:\n    1. Translationese detection runs only when explicitly enabled\n       (`--detect-translationese`).\n    2. When enabled, vocabulary rules for the overlapping terms\n       are SUPPRESSED (not just deduplicated post-hoc) so the\n       translationese detector owns the span.\n    3. Overlap resolution at the span level via existing\n       `src/engine/scan/overlap.rs` machinery.\n  - Scope: new `src/engine/translationese_score.rs`,\n    `src/engine/scan/grammar.rs` (detectors), `assets/ruleset.json`\n    (Phase 1 lexical entries with `source:` metadata),\n    `src/rules/ruleset.rs` (config + new `RuleType::Translationese`\n    variant + all exhaustive-match updates),\n    `src/engine/scan/rule_ir.rs`, `src/engine/scan/spelling.rs`\n    (exhaustive-match updates), `src/main.rs` + `src/mcp/tools.rs`\n    (CLI/MCP flags), `tests/fixtures/translationese/` (with\n    provenance README).\n  - Non-goal: implementing the inverse `westernise` skill\n    (intentional injection of 翻譯腔).  Generation is out of scope\n    for a linter.  Keep as reference for checklist coverage only.",
            "old_string": "### 53.1 Humanize checklist parity — structural & meta AI patterns\n- [ ] Existing 40.x AI writing detection is per-occurrence on\n      `ai_filler` rules (22 vocab entries, C-series signature words).\n      `externals/skills/humanize` formalizes a 26-item checklist\n      covering three axes the current scanner barely touches:\n      structure (S1–S8), vocabulary meta (V3–V6), and formatting\n      (M1–M4).  Adopt the checklist as a linting dimension so zh-TW\n      authors get actionable flags, not just density scores.\n  - Phase 1 — Expand `ai_filler` ruleset with missing vocabulary:\n    C1 grandiose (`舉足輕重`, `里程碑`, `不可磨滅`, `深刻地改變`,\n    `格局`), C2 hollow summary (`綜上所述`, `不可否認`),\n    C3 vague attribution (`廣泛被認為`, `被譽為`, `受到各界關注`),\n    C5 promotional (`坐落於`, `蓬勃發展`, `獨特魅力`,\n    `豐富的文化底蘊`), V1 signature words (`賦能`, `助力`, `打造`,\n    `驅動`, `維度`, `範式`, `奠定基礎`, `深厚的...底蘊`).\n    Gate each with `context_clues` to avoid firing on literal uses\n    (`里程碑` for an actual milestone, `打造` in jewellery context).\n    Tag with existing `RuleType::AiFiller` so `--detect-ai` picks\n    them up automatically.\n  - Phase 2 — New `RuleType::AiStructure` for pattern detectors\n    that exceed lexical matching:\n    - S1 tricolon: detect `A、B、C` triples where items share a\n      register shift (requires segmenter + POS heuristic).  Start\n      with a simpler signature: three identical sentence-final\n      particles or three consecutive `的` clauses in one sentence.\n    - S2 negative parallel: regex-ish match `不(只|僅|僅僅)是.*?(而是|更是)`\n      within a sentence boundary (reuse 37.1 sentence index).\n    - S3 formulaic endings: flag section-terminal sentences\n      matching `展望未來`, `隨著.*不斷發展`, `我們有理由相信`,\n      `拭目以待`.  Requires Markdown heading awareness (35.7).\n    - S5 excessive bold: count `**...**` runs per paragraph in\n      Markdown; flag when density > N per 200 chars.\n    - S6 em-dash overuse: count `——` per paragraph; flag > 1.\n    - S7 formulaic \"despite\": `儘管.*挑戰` + forward-looking verb\n      within one sentence.\n  - Phase 3 — V3 copula avoidance (`作為`, `扮演`, `代表`,\n    `象徵`, `標誌著`) as context-gated ai_filler entries.  Needs\n    negative clues for legitimate uses: `作為` as \"in the capacity\n    of\" remains valid.  Cross-check with existing 38.x `作為` rule\n    if present.\n  - Phase 4 — Meta/formatting (M1–M4): chatbot artifacts\n    (`希望這對你有幫助`, `讓我來為你`), emoji-as-bullet detection,\n    stray Markdown syntax (`**text**` in plaintext outputs).  Most\n    of these fire outside AI filler detection and belong in a\n    new `case` category `ai_meta`.\n  - Reference corpus: `externals/skills/humanize/SKILL.md` Before/After\n    pairs are high-quality evaluation fixtures.  Extract into\n    `tests/fixtures/humanize/` for regression testing.\n  - Interaction with 40.11: structural hits should feed the composite\n    score in `src/engine/ai_score.rs`, not only surface as individual\n    issues.  Structural density > lexical density as an AI signal.\n  - Scope: `assets/ruleset.json` (new entries), `src/rules/ruleset.rs`\n    (new `RuleType::AiStructure`, `ai_meta` case category),\n    `src/engine/scan/grammar.rs` (pattern detectors), `src/engine/\n    ai_score.rs` (composite scoring with structural inputs).\n  - Gate: each of the 26 humanize checklist items maps to ≥1 rule or\n    detector; regression corpus in `tests/fixtures/humanize/`\n    reproduces the expected flag count on Before text and zero flags\n    on After text.\n\n### 53.2 Translationese (`翻譯腔` / 歐化) detection dimension\n- [ ] Currently the scanner has no dedicated detector for Europeanized\n      Chinese syntax.  `externals/skills/dewesternise` provides a\n      25-item checklist distilled from 余光中 and standard 歐化中文\n      literature.  Unlike AI filler detection (which is lexical),\n      翻譯腔 is primarily a syntactic phenomenon: passive voice\n      overuse, abstract subjects, weak-verb decomposition, long\n      pre-modifiers, copula cal