uleType::AiFiller`\n    (no prereqs):\n    - C1 grandiose: `舉足輕重`, `里程碑`, `不可磨滅`, `深刻地改變`,\n      `格局`.\n    - C2 hollow summary: `綜上所述`, `不可否認`, `值得注意的是`,\n      `毫無疑問`.\n    - C3 vague attribution: `廣泛被認為`, `被譽為`, `受到各界關注`,\n      `學者普遍認為`.\n    - C4 superficial analysis: `反映了.*深層` (≤10 chars between),\n      `這一現象的背後`, `結構性變化`.\n    - C5 promotional: `坐落於`, `蓬勃發展`, `獨特魅力`,\n      `豐富的文化底蘊`, `完美融合`, `令人驚豔`.\n    - C7 sycophantic tone: `好問題`, `您說得完全正確`,\n      `非常棒的觀點`.\n    - V1 signature words: `賦能`, `助力`, `打造`, `驅動`, `維度`,\n      `範式`, `奠定基礎`, `深入探討`, `至關重要`, `不可或缺`,\n      `深厚的.*底蘊`.\n    - V2 hedging: `在某種程度上`, `從某個角度來看`, `可以說是`,\n      `相對而言`.  Per-occurrence at `Severity::Info`; density-based\n      flagging is deferred to Phase 2 because it needs paragraph\n      context.\n    - V6 filler phrases: `為了實現這一目標`, `由於.*的事實`,\n      `在這個時間點上`, `具有.*的能力`.\n    Each entry gates with `context_clues`/`negative_context_clues` so\n    literal uses do not fire (`里程碑` for an actual milestone, `打造`\n    in jewellery context, `奠定基礎` in construction context).  Tag\n    with `RuleType::AiFiller` so `--detect-ai` picks them up.\n  - Phase 2 — Structural detectors (BLOCKED on 35.7 + 37.1):\n    - S1 tricolon `A、B、C`: the segmenter is word-boundary only\n      (`src/engine/segment.rs`), no POS.  Implement a punctuation-\n      triggered scanner that walks `、`-separated spans within one\n      sentence (37.1); flag when three spans share identical\n      character length AND identical sentence-final particle, OR\n      when spans match a finite handcrafted register-marker list.\n    - S2 negative parallel: literal substring search for\n      `不只是`/`不僅是`/`不僅僅是` followed within ≤30 chars by\n      `而是`/`更是` in the same sentence (37.1).  Hard cap on the\n      span — no `.*?` regex.\n    - S3 formulaic section endings: flag the last sentence of a\n      Markdown section (35.7) when it matches `展望未來`,\n      `隨著.*不斷發展`, `我們有理由相信`, `拭目以待`, `值得期待`.\n    - S4 mechanical bullet lists: flag a Markdown list (35.7) where\n      every item starts with `**` + keyword + (`**`/`：`/`—`).\n    - S5 excessive bold: count `**...**` runs per Markdown paragraph;\n      flag at ≥3 per 200 chars.\n    - S6 em-dash overuse: count `——` per paragraph; flag at ≥1 per\n      paragraph (source: one per paragraph is already the pattern).\n    - S7 formulaic \"despite\": `儘管.*挑戰` (≤40 chars) + forward-\n      looking verb (`仍然.*發展`, `持續.*繁榮`, `蓬勃發展`) within\n      one sentence (37.1).\n    - S8 false ranges: `從.*到.*再到` chains where the spans are not\n      on a meaningful scale.  Start with a finite list of known\n      false-range openers; require chain to span ≥30 chars.\n    - V2 hedging density: re-evaluate Phase 1 V2 hits at paragraph\n      level; promote `Info` to `Warning` when density exceeds 3 hits\n      per 200 chars.\n  - Phase 3 — V3 copula avoidance: `扮演`, `代表`, `象徵`, `標誌著`\n    as context-gated `ai_filler` entries.  `negative_context_clues`\n    for legitimate uses (`代表` as a noun for a delegate, `象徵`\n    in formal symbolic contexts).  Note: `作為` is OWNED by 53.2.V2\n    (sentence-initial calque) — do NOT add it here.\n  - Phase 4 — Meta/formatting (M1–M4) under context-string\n    discrimination \"AI meta:\":\n    - M1 chatbot artifacts: `希望這對你有幫助`, `讓我來為你`,\n      standalone `以下是` intro lines.\n    - M2 emoji as bullet markers: detect `^[\\p{Emoji}]\\s+\\*\\*` in\n      Markdown list items.\n    - M3 numbered paragraphs that should be prose: flag a numbered\n      list where every item is one sentence and items read as\n      continuous prose (≥3 items, no nested bullets).  Best-effort\n      heuristic.\n    - M4 markup artifacts: `oaicite`, `contentReference`,\n      `turn0search0`, `utm_source=chatgpt.com`, `utm_source=copilot.com`,\n      stray `**text**` in plaintext outputs.  Highest precision and\n      lowest cost — implement first.\n  - Coverage (relaxed gate, with explicit gaps):\n    - Phases 1+3 cover C1–C5, C7, V1, V2, V3 (partial), V6 — 10 of\n      25 items.\n    - Phase 2 covers S1–S8 — 8 of 25 items, after 35.7+37.1 land.\n    - Phase 4 covers M1–M4 — 4 of 25 items.\n    - Total addressable: 22 of 25 (~88%).\n    - Acknowledged gaps: C6 (detail regression — requires comparing\n      a rewrite against its source, out of scope for a single-document\n      linter), V4 (elegant variation — requires document-wide semantic\n      similarity), V5 (present participle chains — Chinese lacks\n      participles; the `了`-chain heuristic is too noisy for first\n      cut).\n    - Per-item mapping table maintained in `assets/ruleset.json` rule\n      metadata (`source: \"humanize.C1\"` etc.) so coverage can be\n      audited mechanically.\n  - Composite score: structural and meta hits feed\n    `src/engine/ai_score.rs` via the context-prefix convention above.\n    No `IssueType` schema change required.  Optional weighting bump\n    for `\"AI structural:\"`-prefixed contexts because structural density\n    is a stronger AI signal than lexical density.\n  - Reference corpus: humanize SKILL.md Before/After pairs into\n    `tests/fixtures/humanize/` with a `README.md` recording upstream\n    commit and license.  Both projects MIT — compatible.\n  - Scope: `assets/ruleset.json` (Phase 1+3+4 entries with `source:`\n    metadata), `src/engine/scan/grammar.rs` (Phase 2 detectors, gated\n    on 35.7+37.1), `src/engine/ai_score.rs` (no schema change; optional\n    weighting bump), `tests/fixtures/humanize/`.\n\n### 53.2 Translationese (`翻譯腔` / 歐化) detection dimension\n- [ ] The scanner has no dedicated detector for Europeanized Chinese\n      syntax.  The dewesternise checklist (25 items: G1–G8, V1–V14,\n      S1–S3) from `externals/skills/dewesternise/SKILL.md` is distilled\n      from 余光中's《論中文之西化》,《從西而不化到西而化之》, and the\n      standard 歐化中文 literature.  Unlike AI filler detection (which\n      is lexical), 翻譯腔 is primarily syntactic: passive voice\n      overuse, abstract subjects, weak-verb decomposition, long\n      pre-modifiers, copula calques.  This warrants a new linting\n      dimension parallel to AI detection.\n  - Naming: `RuleType::Translationese` (matches existing\n    category-noun pattern: `Variant`, `Confusable`, `AiFiller` in\n    `src/rules/ruleset.rs`).  Not `Westernised`/`Westernized`.\n    Module: `src/engine/translationese_score.rs`.\n  - Orthogonality: the translationese score must NOT collapse into\n    the AI score.  A translated technical manual is 歐化 but not\n    AI-generated.  Separate output struct, separate threshold, distinct\n    CLI/MCP field.  Combined `--detect-style` reports the two scores\n    side by side, never as a single number.\n  - Enum strategy: `RuleType::Translationese` is additive serde-side,\n    but every exhaustive `RuleType` match site must be updated in the\n    same commit (`src/rules/ruleset.rs` enum + impls + `From<RuleType>\n    for IssueType`, `src/engine/scan/rule_ir.rs`,\n    `src/engine/scan/spelling.rs`).  Do not split across PRs.\n  - Phase 1 — Lexical detectors (no prereqs):\n    - G5 `們` plural overuse on non-human nouns (`政府們`, `書們`,\n      `國家們`).  `negative_context_clues` for vocatives (`老師們`,\n      `同學們`, `女士們`, `先生們`).  REPORT-ONLY (Phase 4).\n    - G6 `和` overuse: finite list of common verb/adjective pairs\n      (`唱歌和跳舞`, `學習和工作`, `年老和常常生病`).  POS-free.\n    - G7 `當.*的時候` calque: `當` followed within ≤15 chars by\n      `的時候`/`時`.\n    - V1 calque prepositions (sentence-initial only): `關於` at\n      sentence head followed by `,`/`，` within 20 chars; `由於.*\n      的原因` (≤15 chars between); `在.*方面`; `就.*而言`.\n    - V2 `作為一(個|名|位)` at sentence head — \"as a X\".  OWNED\n      by 53.2 (53.1.Phase3 must not duplicate).\n    - V3 `透過` used with abstract means.  `negative_context_clues`:\n      `玻璃`, `縫隙`, `窗戶`, `屏幕`, `布料` (literal \"through\").\n    - V4 `的`-string redundancy (lexical layer only): runs of\n      `X的Y的Z的` ≥3 `的` in one continuous span without internal\n      punctuation.  Distinct from S3 long pre-modifier (which needs\n      sentence index).\n    - V5 `一個` redundancy: `是一個` + adjective.  REPORT-ONLY (Phase 4).\n    - V6 `性` suffix overuse: `(危險|可行|合理|藝術|可能|必要)性`.\n      `negative_context_clues`: `論文`, `研究`, `分析`, `評估`\n      (academic register).\n    - V8 literal adverb: `更好地`, `有效地`, `主要地`, `成功地`,\n      `深入地`.  Gated by following verb.\n    - V9 `這樣一個` outright.\n    - V10 weak verb + nominalization: explicit pair list, not regex.\n      `(進行|展開|作出|給予|加以|予以|提供)` followed within ≤4\n      chars by `(討論|調查|反應|決定|貢獻|檢討|投票|分析|研究|改革|\n      處理|支援|協助)`.  ~40 hand-curated pairs from 余光中.\n      REPORT-ONLY (Phase 4).\n    - V12 `最.*之一`: flag and suggest removing `之一` when no\n      enumeration follows within ≤40 chars.  `negative_context_clues`:\n      `等` after `之一` (citation list context).\n    - V14 existential calques: `有著`, `存在著`, `有.{0,6}的發生`.\n    - S1 semantic overlap: finite list — `提前預告`, `互相合作`,\n      `繼續延續`, `共同協作`, `正在進行中`, `相互交流`, `預先準備`,\n      `事先預告`, `公開公告`.  AUTO-FIX SAFE (exact match).\n    - S2 scientific term overuse: `關注程度`, `重視度`, `強度高`\n      in non-academic prose.  Same academic-register negative clues\n      as V6.\n  - Phase 2 — Syntactic detectors (BLOCKED on 35.7 + 37.1):\n    - G1 passive voice density: count `被` per paragraph; flag at\n      density >2 per 100 chars.  Per-occurrence flagging only when\n      the surrounding verb has a natural active rewrite (`被廣泛\n      認為`, `被視為`, `被稱為`).  WHITELIST (technical zh-TW):\n      `被定義為`, `被廣泛採用`, `被置於`, `被稱作`, `被觀察到`,\n      `被記錄為`.  Configurable per `--profile`.\n    - G2 abstract subject: noun phrase ending in `的(減少|增加|提高|\n      下降|通過|實施)` at sentence head followed by `導致|標誌著|\n      意味著`.  Requires sentence boundary (37.1).\n    - G3/G4 displaced conditionals: `如果.*的話` or `(如果|假如|若)`\n      after the main clause within one sentence (37.1).  Suggest\n      fronting.\n    - G8 pronoun overuse: ≥3 consecutive sentences in one paragraph\n      beginning with `他`/`她`/`它`/`他們`.  Density check.  Requires\n      paragraph index (37.1).\n    - Y1 (余光中, copula+classifier inflation, NOT in dewesternise\n      numbering): `他是一(個|名|位).*?的.*人` within one sentence —\n      flag and suggest deletion of copula+classifier.\n    - Y2 (余光中, `的`/`地` confusion): adjective + `的` + verb\n      where `地` is correct.  Finite list of common confusions\n      (`仔細的看`, `認真的聽`, `慢慢的走`).\n    - S3 `的的不休` (余光中): recursive `的` counter within one\n      sentence (37.1) with no comma between — flag at ≥4 `的` in\n      one continuous span.\n    - V7 `.地` overuse on disyllabic adverbs (`慢慢地`, `靜靜地`,\n      `認真地`).  Finite whitelist.  AUTO-FIX SAFE on the whitelist\n      only.\n    - V13 tense marker overuse: multiple `(曾|已|過|了)` in one\n      sentence when an explicit date is already present.  Density\n      check.\n  - Phase 3a — Scoring module (BLOCKED on 35.7 + 37.1 + Phase 2):\n    new `src/engine/translationese_score.rs`.  Composite from passive\n    density, `的`-chain depth, weak-verb count, pronoun density per\n    1000 chars.  Per-domain calibration: `technical`, `literary`,\n    `news` profiles with different thresholds.  Orthogonal to\n    `ai_score.rs` — separate output struct, separate weight tuning.\n  - Phase 3b — CLI surface: `lint --detect-translationese` (parallel\n    to `--detect-ai`); combined `--detect-style` runs both with two\n    score blocks; `--profile=technical|literary|news` selects domain\n    calibration.\n  - Phase 3c — MCP + ruleset config: MCP `zhtw` tool option\n    `detect_translationese: bool`, separate from `detect_ai`.\n    `translationese_detection: bool` in `src/rules/ruleset.rs` config,\n    default off.  `RuleType::Translationese` variant addition lands\n    here with all match-arm updates in the same commit.\n  - Phase 4 — Fixer integration (narrow auto-fix surface):\n    - AUTO-FIX SAFE (whitelist-only): `V7 地` drop on the disyllabic-\n      adverb whitelist; `V9 這樣一個` → `這麼`; `S1` semantic\n      overlap pairs (exact match).\n    - REPORT-ONLY (context-dependent, both reviewers agreed):\n      `G5 們` (non-human noun detection needs POS), `V5 一個`\n      (mandatory in counting contexts: `只有一個`, `第一個`),\n      `V10` weak-verb collapses (collocational, rhythm-sensitive),\n      all Phase 2 syntactic detectors.\n    - Ship `auto_fix_safe: false` on the report-only set with a\n      `suggested_rewrite` field the user applies manually.\n  - Phase 5 (deferred) — V11 vocabulary blunting via a synonym\n    thesaurus.  Out of scope for the initial cut; needs paired\n    synonym data the project does not have.\n  - Coverage (relaxed gate, with explicit gaps):\n    - Phase 1 covers G5, G6, G7, V1, V2, V3, V4, V5, V6, V8, V9,\n      V10, V12, V14, S1, S2 — 16 of 25 items.\n    - Phase 2 covers G1, G2, G3, G4, G8, S3, V7, V13 — 8 additional\n      items.  Plus Y1 + Y2 余光中 markers (out-of-checklist\n      additions).\n    - Phase 1 + Phase 2 cover 24 of 25 items (~96%).\n    - Acknowledged gaps: V11 (vocabulary blunting) deferred to Phase 5.\n    - Per-item mapping table maintained in `assets/ruleset.json`\n      metadata (`source: \"dewesternise.G1\"`, `source: \"yu.Y1\"`).\n    - Final gate: `--detect-translationese` on a clean zh-TW technical\n      document (project README, technical spec) produces ≤1 false\n      positive per 1000 characters under the `technical` profile.\n  - Reference corpus: dewesternise SKILL.md Before/After pairs (MIT,\n    tzengyuxio/skills) into `tests/fixtures/translationese/` with a\n    `README.md` recording upstream commit and license.  Do NOT ship\n    余光中's copyrighted text — paraphrase canonical examples only,\n    cite the essays as theoretical grounding in code comments.\n  - Existing-rule overlap: I checked `assets/ruleset.json` —\n    `作為`, `透過`, `被` exist only as suggestion targets (`to:`),\n    NOT as flagged sources (`from:`).  No double-flagging mitigation\n    needed.  Translationese detection owns these patterns outright.\n  - Scope: new `src/engine/translationese_score.rs`,\n    `src/engine/scan/grammar.rs` (detectors), `assets/ruleset.json`\n    (Phase 1 lexical entries with `source:` metadata),\n    `src/rules/ruleset.rs` (config + new `RuleType::Translationese`\n    variant + all exhaustive-match updates),\n    `src/engine/scan/rule_ir.rs`, `src/engine/scan/spelling.rs`\n    (exhaustive-match updates), `src/main.rs` + `src/mcp/tools.rs`\n    (CLI/MCP flags), `tests/fixtures/translationese/`.\n  - Non-goal: implementing the inverse `westernise` skill (intentional\n    injection of 翻譯腔).  Generation is out of scope for a linter.\n\n### 53.x prerequisites: 35.7 and 37.1 lifted from P3\n\n53.1 Phase 2 and 53.2 Phase 2 both require structural context the\nscanner does not have:\n- Sentence + paragraph boundary index — currently 37.1 (P3, open).\n- Markdown section / heading awareness — currently 35.7 (P3, partial:\n  exclusion zones only).\n\nWhile 53.x is the active initiative, treat 35.7 and 37.1 as P1-tier\nwork.  Their sections in P3 remain the source of truth for\nimplementation detail; this note tracks the priority lift.  The\nlexical-only sub-phases (53.1.Phase 1+3+4, 53.2.Phase 1) ship without\neither prerequisite and should land first.\n\n---\n\n## P1: Performance & Instrumentation",
